      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Emotional-painful stress and alcohol intoxication activated carboxypeptidase H in the rat pituitary gland. The enzymatic activity was lower in chronic emotional-painful stress and alcohol consumption than that of their single exposure, but higher than that in control rats. In blood serum carboxypeptidase H-like activity was increased after the single emotional-painful stress, while it decreased in chronic stress. Ethanol affected the enzymatic activity in blood serum less significantly than in the pituitary gland."},
